================================================================================
RosettaSciIO (the oracle, and the rules the adapters port)
================================================================================

The DM and Velox signal adapters (Sources/FormatoDM/DMSignals.swift, Sources/
FormatoEMD/VeloxImageSignals.swift) port RosettaSciIO's file readers' rules for
shapes, axes, names, navigation, signal types and the mapped metadata
(rsciio/digitalmicrograph/_api.py, rsciio/emd/_emd_velox.py, rsciio/utils/
_units.py at commit 049e7d7070e84779b499adaf3295beee9facb004), and every reader
is compared with RosettaSciIO's reading of the same files (tools/step-1/pins.py).
The Velox reader moved from SpectroKit follows RosettaSciIO's reading of the
format too. Tests/FormatoDMTests/Fixtures/rsciio-EELS_SI.dm4 is RosettaSciIO's
public test file rsciio/tests/data/digitalmicrograph/3D/EELS_SI.dm4 (sha256
f9b8203f384cc355437594b649d4ea3a12cddeb231ebb65508a841a379fa171a), copied byte
for byte; the JSON pins under Tests/FormatoCoreTests/Fixtures are RosettaSciIO's
readings of its public test files.

